From 3c67f12f7cad56ff56871424cae8b7951abb8124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfry <belfry@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 21:20:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Belfry: Open Source Village branding, deployment relays,
 managed-key sign-in, NIP-42

- OSV dark palette and lime accent as defaults, Geist and favicon from the deployment's /brand,
  OSV logo and titles.
- Relays from the build: VITE_TEST_RELAY (community relay), VITE_SIGNER_RELAYS (Keycast's NIP-46
  relay for nostrconnect).
- Sign-in dialog: the remote signer first, with a hint to the apps page (Connect to Nostr App);
  local keys (existing key, create account) only with VITE_LOCAL_KEYS=true.
- Sidebar: Apps opens VITE_APPS_URL, About goes to VITE_ABOUT_URL; Formstr's privacy policy and
  contact form are hidden when VITE_APPS_URL is set.
- @formstr/local-relay 0.6.0 -> 0.6.5: 0.6.0 never answers NIP-42 AUTH challenges (the app
  already routes them to the signer), so a relay that requires AUTH refused every read and
  write.
